cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "cpgdirection: Predict the Direction of CpG-Gene Expression Associations"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Ein-Dor
    given-names: Tsachi
    email: teindor@runi.ac.il
    affiliation: "Reichman University"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3078-7591"
version: 0.99.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/teindor/cpgdirection"
abstract: >-
  Assigns a direction to the association between DNA methylation at a CpG site
  and the expression of a nearby gene, for CpGs with no measured eQTM record,
  from a precomputed table of 3,105,697 CpG-gene pairs covering 761,445 CpGs.
  Each call returns a direction, a calibrated probability, an evidence tier and
  an expected accuracy, and abstains where the evidence is insufficient.
keywords:
  - DNA methylation
  - gene expression
  - eQTM
  - epigenetics
  - annotation
